Computer Vision – Definition

Computer Vision (CV) is a branch of Artificial Intelligence (AI) that enables computers to capture, analyze, and understand images and videos, allowing them to identify objects, people, text, and activities, similar to how humans use their vision.

Simple Definition:

Computer Vision is a technology that enables computers to "see" and understand visual information from images and videos.

PURPOSE:
👤 Detecting and recognizing people, faces, and objects.
📱 Identifying specific objects, such as a mobile phone or camera.
🚗 Monitoring and analyzing real-time environments.
🔒 Improving security and surveillance systems.
🏥 Assisting in healthcare through medical image analysis.
🤖 Enabling automation in robotics and smart systems.
🚘 Supporting autonomous vehicles by recognizing roads, traffic signs, and pedestrians.
